3,5 $ Non  (On woody substrate) . 5.
4,0 $  Apothecia short-stipitate, errumpent through outer bark, densely aggregated, margin at maturity often splitting, apothecia arising from a stroma embedded in the inner cortex of its hosts, ascospores unicellular .$ Encoelia
4,0 $ Apothecia long-stipitate, one to several arising from an indeterminate stroma, ascospores becoming septate and multicellular at maturity, often with secondary spores produced at the poles .$ Rutstroemia
5,6$  On cones of conifers . 6.
5,7 $ NON ( On cones of conifers)  . . . 7
6,0$ Apothecia dark olive-green, short-stipitate, cup discoid, many apothecia scattered on intact cones. . . .$Piceomphale (excluded from the families)]
6,0 $ Apothecia brown, short-stipitate, cupulate to discoid, one to many from cone-scales of Abies .$Ciboria  rufofusca
7,0 $ On stromatized, decaying catkins. . . .$Ciboria
