10,0 $  Stroma formed superficially on a variety of fruits and berries, associated with a macroconidial anamorphic state of the Botrytis type . .$ Botryotinia
10,11 $ Stroma formed within fruits and berries . 11.
11,0 $ Stroma formed within stone and pome-fruits of the family Rosaceae, associated with a macroconidial anamorphic state of the Monilia type .$ Monilinia
11,12 $ Stroma formed within fruits of Ericaceae, Empetraceae and Pyrolaceae, Monilia anamorph with disjunctors, appearing on foliage 2-4 weeks after apothecial (teleomorphic) state  12.
12,0 $ Stroma formed within fruits of Vaccinium hosts, apothecia long stipitate, ascospores di- or trimorphic $ Franquinia
12,0 $ Stroma on other ericaceous hosts, ascospores usually monomorphic $ Franquinia
